 In this lecture, we want to learn about Amazon Bedrock Architecture.

2
00:00:03,760 --> 00:00:07,120
 So, if you build any application on AWS,

3
00:00:07,120 --> 00:00:11,360
 you know there are two ways in which you can provision AWS services.

4
00:00:11,360 --> 00:00:14,680
 One way is within your AWS account, within your VPC,

5
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:18,640
 you can provision services like EC2 RDS.

6
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:24,960
 And then there is another approach where services like AWS Lambda function, API Gateway,

7
00:00:24,960 --> 00:00:30,880
 which are deployed in AWS service account within AWS VPC.

8
00:00:30,880 --> 00:00:33,840
 And Amazon Bedrock falls in the second category.

9
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:42,320
 So, if you see here, Amazon Bedrock is deployed in the AWS Bedrock Service account.

10
00:00:42,320 --> 00:00:44,560
 So, that's the first thing to note.

11
00:00:44,560 --> 00:00:51,520
 Then we have the second AWS account where we have the model provider escrow account.

12
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:54,640
 And this is AWS owned and operated.

13
00:00:54,640 --> 00:00:58,960
 So, this is where models from different service providers are hosted.

14
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:04,400
 So, let's say we have another topic model and the artifacts of those base model

